                <pb facs="0603" n="1281" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1281"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Nelson to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Santiago de Chili</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 1, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Upon the 30th ultimo I addressed the
                    secretary of foreign relations a note, having for its object a frank exposition
                    of what I deemed the sentiments of the government of the United States towards
                    the other American republics. In preparing this note, a copy of which is
                    herewith transmitted, I availed myself of the views expressed in your despatch
                    No. 14, of June 19, 1862, and in the correspondence submitted by you to the
                    President, under date of April 14, in compliance with the resolution of the
                    House of Representatives of February 3, 1862.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of the United
                            States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d530-a1.xml" xpointer="d530-a1"/>
